---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import { breadcrumbSchema, graph, organizationSchema } from '../lib/seo';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy policy', href: '/privacy/' },
];

const schema = graph([
  organizationSchema(),
  breadcrumbSchema(breadcrumbs),
  {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Privacy policy',
    url: `${SITE.url}/privacy/`,
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#website` },
  },
]);
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What data HostScope collects, what it does not collect, how affiliate tracking works, and how to exercise your rights."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  canonical={`${SITE.url}/privacy/`}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  schema={schema}
  updated={new Date('2026-09-10')}
>
  <p class="lead text-[1.125rem] text-ink-700">
    HostScope is a static website. It has no login, no user accounts and no forms that submit data to
    our servers. The amount of personal information we hold is close to nothing, and this page
    explains precisely what that means.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-collect">What we collect</h2>

  <h3>Information you send us</h3>
  <p>
    If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you write. We keep correspondence for
    as long as it is useful for handling corrections and reader questions, and we do not add anyone to
    a mailing list.
  </p>

  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <p>
    Like most websites, our hosting provider and any analytics service we use may record standard
    technical information: IP address, browser type, referring page, pages visited and timestamps.
    This is aggregate data used to understand which articles are useful. It is not linked to your
    identity.
  </p>

  <h3>Information stored in your browser</h3>
  <p>
    We use browser storage for exactly one thing: remembering whether you dismissed the floating offer
    bar, so it does not reappear during the same visit. This is stored in <code>sessionStorage</code>,
    is not transmitted to us, and is cleared when you close the tab.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-do-not-collect">What we do not collect</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>We do not ask for or store payment details. Nothing is sold on this site.</li>
    <li>We do not run user accounts, comments or forums.</li>
    <li>We do not sell, rent or share personal data with third parties for marketing.</li>
    <li>We do not build advertising profiles.</li>
    <li>We do not use cross-site tracking pixels to follow you around the web.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="affiliate-tracking">How affiliate tracking works</h2>

  <p>
    When you click a Hostinger link on this site, the link includes our affiliate identifier and a
    placement tag. Hostinger and its affiliate network use that to attribute the visit and, if you
    buy, to pay us a commission. If you then purchase, Hostinger may set cookies on its own domain as
    part of its checkout and affiliate attribution process.
  </p>

  <p>
    Once you leave this site, Hostinger's privacy policy governs what happens to your data. We do not
    receive your name, email address or order details — the affiliate network reports aggregate
    numbers such as clicks and conversions, not personal information.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you prefer not to be tracked, use your browser's private mode, a tracker blocker, or simply
    visit hostinger.com directly. You will pay the same price.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>

  <p>
    HostScope itself does not set advertising or profiling cookies. Any cookies you encounter on this
    site would come from third-party services embedded in a page, such as an analytics script or a
    font provider. The site loads fonts from Google Fonts, which may see your IP address and user
    agent as part of serving the font files.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-parties">Third-party services</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Service</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
        <th>What it sees</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Website host / CDN</td>
        <td>Serving the pages</td>
        <td>IP address, request metadata, standard server logs</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Google Fonts</td>
        <td>Loading the Inter typeface</td>
        <td>IP address, user agent</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Hostinger affiliate network</td>
        <td>Attributing referrals</td>
        <td>Click events, referral identifier, aggregate conversions</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="your-rights">Your rights</h2>

  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights under the GDPR, UK GDPR, CCPA or similar
    legislation to access, correct, delete or restrict processing of your personal data. Because we
    hold almost no personal data, in practice this usually means email correspondence. To make a
    request, contact{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.publisher.email}`}>{SITE.publisher.email}</a> and we will respond within 30
    days.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>

  <p>
    This site is aimed at people making business and personal website decisions. It is not directed at
    children under 16 and we do not knowingly collect data from them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>

  <p>
    If this policy changes materially, the "last updated" date at the top of this page will change and
    the substance of the change will be described here.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.publisher.email}`}>{SITE.publisher.email}</a>
    <br />
    {SITE.publisher.legalName}, {SITE.publisher.address}
  </p>
</PageLayout>
